usage: extract_patch_non_inventory.py [-h] [--check] [--self-test]
                                      [--patch PATCH] [--preserve-examples]
                                      [--normalize-inventory-headings]
                                      [--retain-reference-notes]
                                      [--legacy-api-tables]
                                      [--legacy-api-bullets] [--text-only]
                                      [--legacy-cvar-tables] [--bfa-prepatch]
                                      [--legion-prepatch]
                                      [--retain-patch-diff-reference]
                                      [--canonical-patch-navigation]
                                      [--mists-automated-diff]
                                      [--lowercase-reflist]
                                      [--cataclysm-labeled-inventory]
                                      [--mists-source-markup]
                                      [--wrath-summary-markup]
                                      [--numbered-reflist]
                                      [--retail-tbc-markup]
                                      [--retail-240-summary]

Extract retained patch non-inventory wikitext and seed supplemental rows. No
network or dependencies. Line suffixes refer to the generated plaintext,
including blank lines, as in the 12.1.0 page ledger. --check never writes. The
12.0.0 capture has no Notes/Blue posts; 12.0.1 retains Blue posts. Linked
pages are not expanded. --text-only never accesses a coverage ledger.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --check
  --self-test
  --patch PATCH
  --preserve-examples   Retain Lua/XML syntaxhighlight contents verbatim in
                        fenced blocks
  --normalize-inventory-headings
                        Recognize spaced inventory headings without swallowing
                        earlier deprecated tables
  --retain-reference-notes
                        Retain inline ref web citation fields alongside
                        publication prose
  --legacy-api-tables   Strip older caption inventories while retaining API
                        prose and references
  --legacy-api-bullets  Strip legacy API/event bullets without losing prose or
                        unknown markers
  --text-only           Write/check plaintext only; never read or modify a
                        coverage ledger
  --legacy-cvar-tables  Strip CVar inventory tables, retaining
                        captions/citations; opt-in
  --bfa-prepatch        Strip 8.0.1 nested additions/events, retaining prose
                        and reference fields; opt-in
  --legion-prepatch     Strip pure nested Legion inventories, retaining
                        summaries and renames; opt-in
  --retain-patch-diff-reference
                        Retain transcluded patch diffs as unexpanded source
                        references; opt-in
  --canonical-patch-navigation
                        Render positional apichanges patch after named
                        parameters; opt-in
  --mists-automated-diff
                        Strip 2013 Mists API tables while retaining prose and
                        enums; opt-in
  --lowercase-reflist   Retain lowercase reflist as an unexpanded reference
                        marker; opt-in
  --cataclysm-labeled-inventory
                        Strip explicit NEW/REMOVED rows, retain breaking
                        prose/build context; opt-in
  --mists-source-markup
                        Retain Mists external-link fields and omit noinclude
                        wrappers; opt-in
  --wrath-summary-markup
                        Keep 2009 summary attribution and inline Button XML;
                        opt-in
  --numbered-reflist    Retain numbered Reflist markers without expanding
                        citations; opt-in
  --retail-tbc-markup   Keep 2008 retail placeholders/nested citation fields;
                        opt-in
  --retail-240-summary  Keep full mixed 2008 Retail source literally, without
                        linked expansion; opt-in
